{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you are using TanStack Devtools in a React application, we recommend using the React Adapter. The React Adapter provides a set of easy-to-use hooks on top of the core Devtools utilities. If you find yourself wanting to use the core Devtools classes/functions directly, the React Adapter will also re-export everything from the core package."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/react-devtools","lang":"sh"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"component-tanstackdevtools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Component: TanStackDevtools"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The main React component for rendering devtools. It accepts a single props object of type "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackDevtoolsReactInit"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prop"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"plugins"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackDevtoolsReactPlugin[]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Array of plugins to display in the devtools panel"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"config"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackDevtoolsReactConfig"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Devtools UI configuration (position, hotkeys, theme, custom trigger, etc.)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"eventBusConfig"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ClientEventBusConfig"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Event bus connection settings for communicating with the server bus"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"plugin-type-tanstackdevtoolsreactplugin","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Plugin Type: TanStackDevtoolsReactPlugin"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each plugin describes a tab in the devtools panel:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"type PluginRender =\n  | JSX.Element\n  | ((el: HTMLElement, props: TanStackDevtoolsPluginProps) => JSX.Element)\n\ntype TanStackDevtoolsReactPlugin = {\n  id?: string\n  name: string | PluginRender\n  render: PluginRender\n  defaultOpen?: boolean\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"render"}]},{"type":"text","value":" can be a JSX element (simplest -- just pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<YourPanel />"},{"type":"text","value":") or a function that receives the container element and current "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ theme, devtoolsOpen }"},{"type":"text","value":" props. The function form is useful when you need to access the raw DOM element or respond to plugin state changes."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"}]},{"type":"text","value":" works the same way -- use a string for plain text, or JSX / a function for custom tab titles."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is an optional unique identifier. If omitted, it is generated from the name."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultOpen"}]},{"type":"text","value":" marks the plugin as initially active when no other plugins are open."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"usage-example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Usage Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/react-devtools'\nimport { ReactQueryDevtoolsPanel } from '@tanstack/react-query-devtools'\n\nfunction App() {\n  return (\n    <>\n      <YourApp />\n      <TanStackDevtools\n        config={{ position: 'bottom-right', hideUntilHover: true }}\n        eventBusConfig={{ connectToServerBus: true }}\n        plugins={[\n          {\n            name: 'TanStack Query',\n            render: <ReactQueryDevtoolsPanel />,\n            defaultOpen: true,\n          },\n        ]}\n      />\n    </>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"rsc-compatibility","children":[{"type":"text","value":"RSC Compatibility"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The adapter includes a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'use client'"},{"type":"text","value":" directive at the top of its entry file, making it compatible with React Server Components. You can import it directly in your client components without needing to add your own "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'use client'"},{"type":"text","value":" boundary."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"exports","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Exports"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/react-devtools"},{"type":"text","value":" package exports:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackDevtools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" -- the main component"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackDevtoolsReactPlugin"}]},{"type":"text","value":" -- type for plugin objects"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackDevtoolsReactInit"}]},{"type":"text","value":" -- type for the component's props"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"component-tanstackdevtools","text":"Component: TanStackDevtools","level":2},{"id":"plugin-type-tanstackdevtoolsreactplugin","text":"Plugin Type: TanStackDevtoolsReactPlugin","level":2},{"id":"usage-example","text":"Usage Example","level":2},{"id":"rsc-compatibility","text":"RSC Compatibility","level":2},{"id":"exports","text":"Exports","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nIf you are using TanStack Devtools in a React application, we recommend using the React Adapter. The React Adapter provides a set of easy-to-use hooks on top of the core Devtools utilities. If you find yourself wanting to use the core Devtools classes/functions directly, the React Adapter will also re-export everything from the core package.\n\n## Installation\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/react-devtools\n```\n\n## Component: TanStackDevtools\n\nThe main React component for rendering devtools. It accepts a single props object of type `TanStackDevtoolsReactInit`:\n\n| Prop | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `plugins` | `TanStackDevtoolsReactPlugin[]` | Array of plugins to display in the devtools panel |\n| `config` | `TanStackDevtoolsReactConfig` | Devtools UI configuration (position, hotkeys, theme, custom trigger, etc.) |\n| `eventBusConfig` | `ClientEventBusConfig` | Event bus connection settings for communicating with the server bus |\n\n## Plugin Type: TanStackDevtoolsReactPlugin\n\nEach plugin describes a tab in the devtools panel:\n\n```ts\ntype PluginRender =\n  | JSX.Element\n  | ((el: HTMLElement, props: TanStackDevtoolsPluginProps) => JSX.Element)\n\ntype TanStackDevtoolsReactPlugin = {\n  id?: string\n  name: string | PluginRender\n  render: PluginRender\n  defaultOpen?: boolean\n}\n```\n\n- **`render`** can be a JSX element (simplest -- just pass `<YourPanel />`) or a function that receives the container element and current `{ theme, devtoolsOpen }` props. The function form is useful when you need to access the raw DOM element or respond to plugin state changes.\n- **`name`** works the same way -- use a string for plain text, or JSX / a function for custom tab titles.\n- **`id`** is an optional unique identifier. If omitted, it is generated from the name.\n- **`defaultOpen`** marks the plugin as initially active when no other plugins are open.\n\n## Usage Example\n\n```tsx\nimport { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/react-devtools'\nimport { ReactQueryDevtoolsPanel } from '@tanstack/react-query-devtools'\n\nfunction App() {\n  return (\n    <>\n      <YourApp />\n      <TanStackDevtools\n        config={{ position: 'bottom-right', hideUntilHover: true }}\n        eventBusConfig={{ connectToServerBus: true }}\n        plugins={[\n          {\n            name: 'TanStack Query',\n            render: <ReactQueryDevtoolsPanel />,\n            defaultOpen: true,\n          },\n        ]}\n      />\n    </>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## RSC Compatibility\n\nThe adapter includes a `'use client'` directive at the top of its entry file, making it compatible with React Server Components. You can import it directly in your client components without needing to add your own `'use client'` boundary.\n\n## Exports\n\nThe `@tanstack/react-devtools` package exports:\n\n- **`TanStackDevtools`** -- the main component\n- **`TanStackDevtoolsReactPlugin`** -- type for plugin objects\n- **`TanStackDevtoolsReactInit`** -- type for the component's props\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: TanStack Devtools React Adapter\nid: adapter\n---\n\nIf you are using TanStack Devtools in a React application, we recommend using the React Adapter. The React Adapter provides a set of easy-to-use hooks on top of the core Devtools utilities. If you find yourself wanting to use the core Devtools classes/functions directly, the React Adapter will also re-export everything from the core package.\n\n## Installation\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/react-devtools\n```\n\n## Component: TanStackDevtools\n\nThe main React component for rendering devtools. It accepts a single props object of type `TanStackDevtoolsReactInit`:\n\n| Prop | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `plugins` | `TanStackDevtoolsReactPlugin[]` | Array of plugins to display in the devtools panel |\n| `config` | `TanStackDevtoolsReactConfig` | Devtools UI configuration (position, hotkeys, theme, custom trigger, etc.) |\n| `eventBusConfig` | `ClientEventBusConfig` | Event bus connection settings for communicating with the server bus |\n\n## Plugin Type: TanStackDevtoolsReactPlugin\n\nEach plugin describes a tab in the devtools panel:\n\n```ts\ntype PluginRender =\n  | JSX.Element\n  | ((el: HTMLElement, props: TanStackDevtoolsPluginProps) => JSX.Element)\n\ntype TanStackDevtoolsReactPlugin = {\n  id?: string\n  name: string | PluginRender\n  render: PluginRender\n  defaultOpen?: boolean\n}\n```\n\n- **`render`** can be a JSX element (simplest -- just pass `<YourPanel />`) or a function that receives the container element and current `{ theme, devtoolsOpen }` props. The function form is useful when you need to access the raw DOM element or respond to plugin state changes.\n- **`name`** works the same way -- use a string for plain text, or JSX / a function for custom tab titles.\n- **`id`** is an optional unique identifier. If omitted, it is generated from the name.\n- **`defaultOpen`** marks the plugin as initially active when no other plugins are open.\n\n## Usage Example\n\n```tsx\nimport { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/react-devtools'\nimport { ReactQueryDevtoolsPanel } from '@tanstack/react-query-devtools'\n\nfunction App() {\n  return (\n    <>\n      <YourApp />\n      <TanStackDevtools\n        config={{ position: 'bottom-right', hideUntilHover: true }}\n        eventBusConfig={{ connectToServerBus: true }}\n        plugins={[\n          {\n            name: 'TanStack Query',\n            render: <ReactQueryDevtoolsPanel />,\n            defaultOpen: true,\n          },\n        ]}\n      />\n    </>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## RSC Compatibility\n\nThe adapter includes a `'use client'` directive at the top of its entry file, making it compatible with React Server Components. You can import it directly in your client components without needing to add your own `'use client'` boundary.\n\n## Exports\n\nThe `@tanstack/react-devtools` package exports:\n\n- **`TanStackDevtools`** -- the main component\n- **`TanStackDevtoolsReactPlugin`** -- type for plugin objects\n- **`TanStackDevtoolsReactInit`** -- type for the component's props\n"}
